From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 02:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rzg2l: report the kaslr-seed outcome on the console

ft_board_setup() seeds /chosen/kaslr-seed from the OP-TEE RNG. Upstream
writes it inside a compound condition, so every failure path is silent:
if the RNG is unavailable or the read fails, the kernel boots without
ASLR and nothing says so.

Split the condition and state the outcome either way, in the same
[EDGE] marker format the boot chain uses elsewhere, so a captured serial
log shows whether ASLR was seeded rather than leaving it to inference.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific console instrumentation]

Signed-off-by: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
---
 board/renesas/rcar-common/common.c | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/board/renesas/rcar-common/common.c
+++ b/board/renesas/rcar-common/common.c
@@ -245,6 +245,7 @@
 
 int ft_board_setup(void *blob, struct bd_info *bd)
 {
+	int ret;
 	struct udevice *dev;
 	u64 seed;
 	u8 mac[6];
@@ -279,10 +280,16 @@
 	fdt_fixup_ethernet(blob);
 
 	/* Write /chosen/kaslr-seed from OP-TEE RNG for kernel ASLR */
-	if (!uclass_get_device(UCLASS_RNG, 0, &dev) &&
-	    !dm_rng_read(dev, &seed, sizeof(seed)))
-		fdt_setprop(blob, fdt_path_offset(blob, "/chosen"),
-			    "kaslr-seed", &seed, sizeof(seed));
+	ret = uclass_get_device(UCLASS_RNG, 0, &dev);
+	if (ret) {
+		printf("[EDGE] UBOOT kaslr-seed=FAILED rng=unavailable ret=%d\n", ret);
+	} else if (dm_rng_read(dev, &seed, sizeof(seed))) {
+		printf("[EDGE] UBOOT kaslr-seed=FAILED rng=read-error\n");
+	} else {
+		ret = fdt_setprop(blob, fdt_path_offset(blob, "/chosen"),
+				  "kaslr-seed", &seed, sizeof(seed));
+		printf("[EDGE] UBOOT kaslr-seed=%s\n", ret ? "FAILED fdt" : "ok");
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
